>> title: Fried Okra
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: okra, cornmeal, southern, shallow-fry, side
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: fried okra, cornmeal okra, okra rounds, breaded okra
>> servings: 6
>> time: 40 min
>> pairs-with: fried-chicken, collard-greens, skillet-cornbread, stewed-squash
>> step.1: Cut the okra and fry it within the hour. Sliced okra sits and goes ropey.
>> step.2: slice in 1/2-in rounds
>> step.3: toss in buttermilk
>> step.4: whisk the meal
>> step.5: dredge, shake off
>> step.6: fry 5 min, turned once

Cut the okra and fry it within the hour.

Slice @okra{1 1/2%lb}(680 g) into 1/2-in rounds, stem caps discarded.

Toss @&(~1)okra rounds{} in @buttermilk{1%cup}(240 mL) and let them drip.

Whisk @fine yellow cornmeal{1%cup}(140 g), @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup}(65 g), @fine sea salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, @cayenne{1/2%tsp}.

Dredge @&(~2)wet okra{} in @&(~1)seasoned meal{}, shaken off in a sieve.

Fry @&(~1)coated okra{} in @peanut oil{2%cup}(475 mL) at 360°F (180°C) in a #cast-iron skillet{} for ~fry{5%min}.

Salt it the moment it leaves the fat while the surface is still wet. Salted cold it slides straight off.
